# Agent skills are personal tooling, not project source. `.claude/commands/`
# and `.claude/settings.json` stay tracked because they encode repo conventions
# (the release runbook, the git identity hook); skills do not. Vendoring one in
# put 23 files of third-party MIT code in the tree that nothing here imports —
# keep them in `~/.claude/skills/` so they follow the developer, not the repo.
.claude/skills/

# HeoPress 跟踪 OpenSpec 工作流技能（Claude Code 与 Codex 交接共用），覆盖上一条上游规则
